#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"
msgstr "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits are executed on IBM&reg; hardware as sequences of microwave pulses that need to be scheduled and run at precise time intervals.\n"
"Unfortunately, unwanted interactions between qubits can lead to coherent errors on idling qubits. Dynamical decoupling works by inserting pulse sequences on idling qubits to approximately cancel out the effect of these errors. Each inserted pulse sequence amounts to an identity operation, but the physical presence of the pulses has the effect of suppressing errors.\n"
"There are many possible choices of pulse sequences, and which sequence is better for each particular case remains an [active area of research](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.064027).\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar kuantum dilaksanakan pada perkakasan IBM&reg; sebagai urutan nadi gelombang mikro yang perlu dijadualkan dan dijalankan pada selang masa yang tepat.\n"
"Malangnya, interaksi tidak diingini antara qubit boleh membawa kepada ralat koheren pada qubit yang melahu. Dynamical decoupling berfungsi dengan memasukkan urutan nadi pada qubit yang melahu untuk kira-kira membatalkan kesan ralat ini. Setiap urutan nadi yang dimasukkan setara dengan operasi identiti, tetapi kehadiran fizikal nadi tersebut mempunyai kesan menindas ralat.\n"
"Terdapat banyak pilihan urutan nadi yang mungkin, dan urutan mana yang lebih baik untuk setiap kes tertentu masih merupakan [bidang penyelidikan aktif](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.064027).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that dynamical decoupling is mainly useful for circuits containing gaps in which some qubits sit idle without any operations acting on them. If the operations in the circuit are packed very densely, such that all of the qubits are busy most of the time, then the addition of dynamical decoupling pulses might not improve performance. In fact, it could even worsen performance due to imperfections in the pulses themselves.\n"
msgstr "Perlu diingat bahawa dynamical decoupling terutamanya berguna untuk litar yang mengandungi jurang di mana sebahagian qubit duduk melahu tanpa sebarang operasi yang bertindak ke atasnya. Jika operasi dalam litar sangat padat, sedemikian rupa sehingga semua qubit sibuk sebahagian besar masa, maka penambahan nadi dynamical decoupling mungkin tidak meningkatkan prestasi. Malah, ia boleh memburukkan lagi prestasi akibat ketidaksempurnaan dalam nadi itu sendiri.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagram below depicts dynamical decoupling with an XX pulse sequence. The abstract circuit on the left is mapped onto a microwave pulse schedule on the top right. The bottom right depicts the same schedule, but with a sequence of two X pulses inserted during an idle period of the first qubit.\n"
msgstr "Rajah di bawah menggambarkan dynamical decoupling dengan urutan nadi XX. Litar abstrak di sebelah kiri dipetakan ke jadual nadi gelombang mikro di kanan atas. Kanan bawah menggambarkan jadual yang sama, tetapi dengan urutan dua nadi X yang dimasukkan semasa tempoh melahu qubit pertama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of dynamical decoupling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/dd.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran dynamical decoupling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/dd.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling can be enabled by setting `enable` to `True` in the [dynamical decoupling options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-dynamical-decoupling-options). The `sequence_type` option can be used to pick from several different pulse sequences. The default sequence type is `\"XX\"`.\n"
msgstr "Dynamical decoupling boleh didayakan dengan menetapkan `enable` kepada `True` dalam [pilihan dynamical decoupling](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-dynamical-decoupling-options). Pilihan `sequence_type` boleh digunakan untuk memilih dari beberapa urutan nadi yang berbeza. Jenis urutan lalai ialah `\"XX\"`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code cell shows how to enable dynamical decoupling for Estimator and choose a dynamical decoupling sequence.\n"
msgstr "Sel kod berikut menunjukkan cara mendayakan dynamical decoupling untuk Estimator dan memilih urutan dynamical decoupling.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"
msgstr "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirling, also known as [randomized compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325), is a widely used technique for converting arbitrary noise channels into noise channels with more specific structure.\n"
msgstr "Twirling, juga dikenali sebagai [pengkompilan rawak](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325), adalah teknik yang digunakan secara meluas untuk menukar saluran hingar sewenang-wenangnya menjadi saluran hingar dengan struktur yang lebih spesifik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling is a special kind of twirling that uses Pauli operations. It has the effect of transforming any quantum channel into a Pauli channel. Performed alone, it can mitigate coherent noise because coherent noise tends to accumulate quadratically with the number of operations, whereas Pauli noise accumulates linearly. Pauli twirling is often combined with other error mitigation techniques that work better with Pauli noise than with arbitrary noise.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling adalah jenis twirling khas yang menggunakan operasi Pauli. Ia mempunyai kesan mengubah sebarang saluran kuantum menjadi saluran Pauli. Apabila dilakukan sahaja, ia boleh mengurangkan hingar koheren kerana hingar koheren cenderung terkumpul secara kuadratik dengan bilangan operasi, sedangkan hingar Pauli terkumpul secara linear. Pauli twirling sering digabungkan dengan teknik mitigasi ralat lain yang berfungsi lebih baik dengan hingar Pauli berbanding hingar sewenang-wenangnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling is implemented by sandwiching a chosen set of gates with randomly chosen single-qubit Pauli gates in such a way that the ideal effect of the gate remains the same. The result is that a single circuit is replaced with a random ensemble of circuits, all with the same ideal effect. When sampling the circuit, samples are drawn from multiple random instances, rather than just a single one.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling dilaksanakan dengan mengapit set gate yang dipilih dengan gate Pauli satu qubit yang dipilih secara rawak sedemikian rupa sehingga kesan ideal gate tetap sama. Hasilnya ialah satu litar digantikan dengan ensemble rawak litar, semua dengan kesan ideal yang sama. Apabila mensampling litar, sampel diambil dari pelbagai contoh rawak, bukan hanya satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since most of the errors in current quantum hardware come from two-qubit gates, this technique is often applied exclusively to (native) two-qubit gates. The following diagram depicts some Pauli twirls for the CNOT and ECR gates. Every circuit within a row has the same ideal effect.\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana sebahagian besar ralat dalam perkakasan kuantum semasa datang dari gate dua qubit, teknik ini sering diterapkan secara eksklusif pada gate dua qubit (asli). Rajah berikut menggambarkan beberapa Pauli twirl untuk gate CNOT dan ECR. Setiap litar dalam satu baris mempunyai kesan ideal yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of gate twirls](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran twirl gate](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling can be enabled by setting `enable_gates` to `True` in the [twirling options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-twirling-options). Other notable options include:\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling boleh didayakan dengan menetapkan `enable_gates` kepada `True` dalam [pilihan twirling](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-twirling-options). Pilihan penting lain termasuk:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_randomizations`: The number of circuit instances to draw from the ensemble of twirled circuits.\n"
msgstr "`num_randomizations`: Bilangan contoh litar yang hendak diambil dari ensemble litar yang di-twirl.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`shots_per_randomization`: The number of shots to sample from each circuit instance.\n"
msgstr "`shots_per_randomization`: Bilangan shot yang hendak disampling dari setiap contoh litar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code cell shows how to enable Pauli twirling and set these options for Estimator. None of these options are required to be set explicitly.\n"
msgstr "Sel kod berikut menunjukkan cara mendayakan Pauli twirling dan menetapkan pilihan ini untuk Estimator. Tiada satu pun pilihan ini perlu ditetapkan secara eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"
msgstr "Pemadaman Ralat Readout yang di-Twirl (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) mitigates the effect of measurement errors for the estimation of Pauli observable expectation values.\n"
"It is based on the notion of twirled measurements, which are accomplished by randomly substituting measurement gates by a sequence of (1) a Pauli X gate, (2) a measurement, and (3) classical bit flip. Just like in standard gate twirling, this sequence is equivalent to a plain measurement in the absence of noise, as depicted in the following diagram:\n"
msgstr ""
"[Pemadaman Ralat Readout yang di-Twirl (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) mengurangkan kesan ralat pengukuran untuk anggaran nilai jangkaan boleh cerap Pauli.\n"
"Ia berdasarkan konsep pengukuran yang di-twirl, yang dicapai dengan menggantikan gate pengukuran secara rawak dengan urutan (1) gate Pauli X, (2) pengukuran, dan (3) pembalikkan bit klasik. Sama seperti dalam twirling gate standard, urutan ini setara dengan pengukuran biasa tanpa adanya hingar, seperti yang digambarkan dalam rajah berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of measurement twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran pengukuran twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the presence of readout error, measurement twirling has the effect of diagonalizing the readout-error transfer matrix, making it easy to invert. A rescaling term from the diagonal noise channel is learned by\n"
"benchmarking random circuits initialized in the zero state. This allows\n"
"the service to remove bias from expectation values that result from\n"
"readout noise. Estimating the readout-error transfer matrix requires executing additional calibration circuits, which introduces a small overhead.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kehadiran ralat readout, pengukuran twirling mempunyai kesan mendiagonalkan matriks pemindahan ralat readout, menjadikannya mudah untuk disongsangkan. Sebutan penskalan semula dari saluran hingar pepenjuru dipelajari dengan membandingkan litar rawak yang dimulakan dalam keadaan sifar. Ini membolehkan perkhidmatan mengeluarkan berat sebelah daripada nilai jangkaan yang terhasil daripada hingar readout. Menganggar matriks pemindahan ralat readout memerlukan melaksanakan litar kalibrasi tambahan, yang memperkenalkan sedikit overhead.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enable TREX by using the `measure_mitigation` option {#enable-trex-by-using-the-measure-mitigation-option}"
msgstr "Dayakan TREX dengan menggunakan pilihan `measure_mitigation` {#enable-trex-by-using-the-measure-mitigation-option}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "TREX can be enabled by setting `measure_mitigation` to `True` in the [Qiskit Runtime resilience options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-resilience-options-v2) for Estimator. Options for measurement noise learning are described [here](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-measure-noise-learning-options). As with gate twirling, you can set the number of circuit randomizations and the number of shots per randomization.\n"
msgid "TREX can be enabled by setting `measure_mitigation` to `True` in the [IBM Quantum Compute resilience options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-resilience-options-v2) for Estimator. Options for measurement noise learning are described [here](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-measure-noise-learning-options). As with gate twirling, you can set the number of circuit randomizations and the number of shots per randomization.\n"
msgstr "TREX boleh didayakan dengan menetapkan `measure_mitigation` kepada `True` dalam [pilihan ketahanan Qiskit Runtime](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-resilience-options-v2) untuk Estimator. Pilihan untuk pembelajaran hingar pengukuran diterangkan [di sini](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-measure-noise-learning-options). Seperti twirling gate, anda boleh menetapkan bilangan rawak litar dan bilangan shot per rawak.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code cell shows how to enable TREX and set these options for Estimator. None of these options have to be set explicitly.\n"
msgstr "Sel kod berikut menunjukkan cara mendayakan TREX dan menetapkan pilihan ini untuk Estimator. Tiada satu pun pilihan ini perlu ditetapkan secara eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enable TREX by using the `resilience_level` option {#enable-trex-by-using-the-resilience-level-option}"
msgstr "Dayakan TREX dengan menggunakan pilihan `resilience_level` {#enable-trex-by-using-the-resilience-level-option}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can enable TREX by setting the [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) to `1`, as shown in the following example.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh mendayakan TREX dengan menetapkan [tahap ketahanan](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) kepada `1`, seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam contoh berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"
msgstr "Ekstrapolasi sifar-hingar (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is a technique for mitigating errors in estimating expectation values of observables. While it often improves results, it is not guaranteed to produce an unbiased result.\n"
msgstr "Ekstrapolasi sifar-hingar (ZNE) adalah teknik untuk mengurangkan ralat dalam menganggar nilai jangkaan boleh cerap. Walaupun ia sering meningkatkan keputusan, ia tidak dijamin menghasilkan keputusan yang tidak berat sebelah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE consists of two stages:\n"
msgstr "ZNE terdiri daripada dua peringkat:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Noise amplification_: The original quantum circuit is executed multiple times at different noise rates.\n"
msgstr "_Amplifikasi hingar_: Litar kuantum asal dilaksanakan beberapa kali pada kadar hingar yang berbeza.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Extrapolation_: The ideal result is estimated by extrapolating the noisy expectation value results to the zero-noise limit.\n"
msgstr "_Ekstrapolasi_: Keputusan ideal dianggar dengan mengekstrapolasi keputusan nilai jangkaan berhingar ke had sifar-hingar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both the noise amplification and extrapolation stages can be implemented in many different ways. IBM Quantum Compute implements noise amplification by \"digital gate folding,\" which means that two-qubit gates are replaced with equivalent sequences of the gate and its inverse. For example, replacing a unitary $U$ with $U U^\\dagger U$ would yield a noise amplification factor of 3. For the extrapolation, you can choose from one of several functional forms, including a linear fit or an exponential fit.\n"
"The image below depicts digital gate folding on the left, and the extrapolation procedure on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-dua peringkat amplifikasi hingar dan ekstrapolasi boleh dilaksanakan dalam pelbagai cara yang berbeza. IBM Quantum Compute melaksanakan amplifikasi hingar melalui \"pelipatan gate digital,\" yang bermakna gate dua qubit digantikan dengan urutan setara gate tersebut dan inversnya. Contohnya, menggantikan uniter $U$ dengan $U U^\\dagger U$ akan menghasilkan faktor amplifikasi hingar sebanyak 3. Untuk ekstrapolasi, anda boleh memilih dari salah satu daripada beberapa bentuk fungsian, termasuk padanan linear atau padanan eksponen.\n"
"Imej di bawah menggambarkan pelipatan gate digital di sebelah kiri, dan prosedur ekstrapolasi di sebelah kanan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/zne.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/zne.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The overhead of this method scales with the number of noise factors. The\n"
"default settings sample the expectation value at three noise factors,\n"
"leading to a roughly 3x overhead.\n"
msgstr "Overhead kaedah ini berskala dengan bilangan faktor hingar. Tetapan lalai menyampling nilai jangkaan pada tiga faktor hingar, menghasilkan overhead kira-kira 3x.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enable ZNE by using the `zne_mitigation` option {#enable-zne-by-using-the-zne-mitigation-option}"
msgstr "Dayakan ZNE dengan menggunakan pilihan `zne_mitigation` {#enable-zne-by-using-the-zne-mitigation-option}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ZNE can be enabled by setting `zne_mitigation` to `True` in the [IBM Quantum Compute resilience options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-resilience-options-v2) for Estimator.\n"
"The options for ZNE are described [here](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-zne-options). The following options are notable:\n"
msgstr ""
"ZNE boleh didayakan dengan menetapkan `zne_mitigation` kepada `True` dalam [pilihan ketahanan IBM Quantum Compute](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-resilience-options-v2) untuk Estimator.\n"
"Pilihan IBM Quantum Compute untuk ZNE diterangkan [di sini](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-zne-options). Pilihan berikut adalah penting:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`noise_factors`: The noise factors to use for noise amplification.\n"
msgstr "`noise_factors`: Faktor hingar untuk digunakan dalam amplifikasi hingar.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`extrapolator`: The functional form to use for the extrapolation.\n"
msgstr "`extrapolator`: Bentuk fungsian untuk digunakan dalam ekstrapolasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code cell shows how to enable ZNE and set these options for Estimator. None of these options have to be set explicitly.\n"
msgstr "Sel kod berikut menunjukkan cara mendayakan ZNE dan menetapkan pilihan ini untuk Estimator. Tiada satu pun pilihan ini perlu ditetapkan secara eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enable ZNE by using the `resilience_level` option {#enable-zne-by-using-the-resilience-level-option}"
msgstr "Dayakan ZNE dengan menggunakan pilihan `resilience_level` {#enable-zne-by-using-the-resilience-level-option}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can enable ZNE (along with TREX and gate twirling) by setting the [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) to `2`, as shown in the following example.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh mendayakan ZNE (bersama TREX dan gate twirling) dengan menetapkan [tahap ketahanan](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) kepada `2`, seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam contoh berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pea\"></span>\n"
